{"id":459,"name":"snover","speciesId":459,"dex":459,"form":"normal","generation":4,"types":["grass","ice"],"stats":{"hp":60,"attack":62,"defense":50,"special-attack":62,"special-defense":60,"speed":40},"abilities":[{"name":"snow-warning","hidden":false},{"name":"soundproof","hidden":true}],"height":10,"weight":505,"baseExp":67,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/459.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/459.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/459.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/459.ogg","genus":"Frost Tree Pokémon","flavor":[{"version":"diamond","text":"It lives on snowy mountains. Having had little contact with humans, it is boldly inquisitive."},{"version":"pearl","text":"In the spring, it grows berries with the texture of frozen treats around its belly."},{"version":"platinum","text":"Seemingly curious about people, they gather around footsteps they find on snowy mountains."},{"version":"heartgold","text":"During cold seasons, it migrates to the mountain’s lower reaches. It returns to the snow-covered summit in the spring."},{"version":"sword","text":"It lives on snowy mountains. It sinks its legs into the snow to absorb water and keep its own temperature down."},{"version":"shield","text":"The berries that grow around its belly are like ice pops. Galarian Darumaka absolutely love these berries."},{"version":"legends-arceus","text":"One is likely to encounter this Pokémon while out in the snow. There are stories of Snover appearing in human settlements but doing no harm—rather, they bond with the children."}],"genderRate":4,"captureRate":120,"eggGroups":["monster","plant"],"isLegendary":false,"isMythical":false,"evolution":{"species":"snover","speciesId":459,"evolvesTo":[{"conditions":["Nível 40"],"speci